{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4EXwJqfthXXx6n9Snn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The engine's headless loader is simple enough to reuse for a single test command. Before writing the game, I'll pull the club names and cup story beats from the plan so the content matches the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4655,"cache_read_input_tokens":79349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4655},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4140afa2-f753-4694-9098-5b15dffc61f3","uuid":"8d4cd80a-14e6-4201-aee8-9296548b3a3b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:36:54.681Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4EXewTnDJcVWzu8BAd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4EXwJqfthXXx6n9Snn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NyeqBDRzJfWSwsRNKNzxwZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-073543__xcf3323/work && sed -n 1323,1345p PLAN.md; echo ....; grep -n -E '^\\| ?`?[a-z0-9-]+`? ?\\|' PLAN.md | sed -n 1,60p | cut -c1-220; echo ....; sed -n 1439,1470p PLAN.md | cut -c1-400","description":"Read team, story and beat sections of PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4655,"cache_read_input_tokens":79349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4655},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4140afa2-f753-4694-9098-5b15dffc61f3","uuid":"a6488faa-8e16-4121-9eef-7430dbb97ad8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:36:55.707Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4EXewTnDJcVWzu8BAd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NyeqBDRzJfWSwsRNKNzxwZ":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-073543__xcf3323/work && sed -n 1323,1345p PLAN.md; echo ....; grep -n -E '^\\| ?`?[a-z0-9-]+`? ?\\|' PLAN.md | sed -n 1,60p | cut -c1-220; echo ....; sed -n 1439,1470p PLAN.md | cut -c1-400","description":"Read team, story and beat sections of PLAN.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NyeqBDRzJfWSwsRNKNzxwZ","type":"tool_result","content":"### 7.1 Teams\n\nEach team: name, short code, nickname, city, stadium, kits (home, away, keeper), crest, formation, tactic, chant,\nsignature celebration, 5 players (number, name, position, build, size, hair, skin, hair colour, stats, captain's super).\nKit colours give rig colours: `cloth` (shirt), `pants` (shorts), `boot`, `belt` (= shorts), `trim` (socks and collar),\n`glove` (keepers), plus `kit: { pattern, color2, number, numberColor }` (§5.2).\n\n**KIPPERTON ATHLETIC** — \"The Kippers\", KIP. A fishing town on the cold north coast. Home: the Smokehouse. Kit: tangerine\n`#f08a24` and navy `#1c2a5a` hoops, navy shorts, tangerine socks; away: white with a tangerine sash. Crest: a navy shield\nwith a smoked kipper crossed over an anchor. Formation 2-1-1 (the team talk can change it). Tactic `plucky` (balanced:\npress .55, line .45, tempo .7, passRisk .5). Chant \"KIP-PER-TON!\". Celebration: the fish slap. Manager: MAGS MULLIGAN\n(a fishmonger turned manager: flat cap, scarf, a voice like a foghorn).\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Build / size / hair | Key stats | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | WALLY CRABB | GK | bulky 1.2, bald | keep 76, weight 80 | 41, a part-time lighthouse keeper; huge gloves |\n| 4 | SANDRA \"THE HARBOUR WALL\" OKAFOR | DEF | bulky 1.2, short | tackle 88, weight 95, temper 40 | barges like a trawler |\n| 6 | AGGIE NOWAK | MID | heroic 1.12, ponytail | pass 90, skill 70 | the brains; Polish grandmother in the stands |\n| 7 | TOMMY \"TWINKLETOES\" TRAN | FWD | heroic 1.08, spiky | pace 95, skill 92 | step-overs for breakfast |\n| 9 | DAZ PILCHARD (captain) | FWD | heroic 1.15, short | shoot 90, pace 80 | super **THE SMOKED KIPPER** (path `wobble`, smoke trail, the ball briefly shaped like a fish) |\n\n**AFC HOOFINGTON** — \"The Hoofers\", HOO (Qualifying Round). Brown `#6a4a2a` and amber `#e8a830` stripes. Crest: a\nmuddy boot. Formation 2-2. Tactic `routeone` (longBall .6, press .4, line .4, tempo .5, foul .25). Chant: a\n....\n11:|---|---|\n77:|---|---|\n98:|---|---|---|\n119:|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n120:| move | run / dribble | run | L-stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n121:| `sprint` | sprint (stamina) | sprint | R2 / RT (`Pad7`) | Left Shift | — |\n122:| `pass` | ground pass to the teammate the stick points at | standing tackle (poke) | ✕ / A (`Pad0`) | J | Left click: pass toward the cursor (click a teammate to pass to them) |\n123:| `shoot` | hold to charge, release to shoot; stick aims | slide tackle | □ / X (`Pad2`) | K | Right button held: charge, release to shoot at the cursor |\n124:| `lob` | lob, cross from wide, chip near the keeper | shoulder barge | ○ / B (`Pad1`) | L | Middle click: lob toward the cursor |\n125:| `through` | through ball into space | switch player | △ / Y (`Pad3`) | I | — |\n126:| `skill` | skill move (by stick direction, §6.6) | — | R1 / RB (`Pad5`) | E | — |\n127:| `switch` | hold with pass: one-two | switch to the teammate nearest the ball | L1 / LB (`Pad4`) | Q | Left click on a teammate while defending: switch to them |\n128:| `dive` | Theatrics (dive) | Theatrics | L2 / LT (`Pad6`) | C | — |\n129:| `euphoria` | trigger Europhoria when the meter is full | same | L1 + R1 together | Space (also Q + E) | — |\n130:| pause | pause menu (engine) | | Options (`Pad9`) | Esc, P | the corner's menu button |\n320:|---|---|---|\n426:|---|---|---|---|---|\n641:|---|---|---|---|\n698:|---|---|\n707:| decay | −`EF.T.euphoriaDecay` (1.5) per second when above 0 and not in Europhoria |\n843:|---|---|---|---|---|\n1007:|---|---|---|\n1008:| `anthem` | title, tunnel walkout, trophy ceremony | the EUROPHORIA ANTHEM: a grand cup-competition anthem in its own melody (Appendix D) |\n1009:| `menu` | menus, setup, album | an upbeat 128 bpm loop on the anthem's chords |\n1010:| `travel` | the travel map | a jaunty road-trip tune (whistled lead: sine with vibrato) |\n1011:| `tabloid` | tabloid screens | a press-room stinger and a short loop (typewriter ticks in the drums) |\n1012:| `dressing` | team talks | a warm low loop |\n1013:| `europhoria` | in the match, as a layer | drums, brass stabs and bass, faded in by `audio.layer` during Europhoria; otherwise matches have no music, only the crowd |\n1014:| `halftime` | the half-time overlay | a light jazzy jingle |\n1015:| `goal` | `audio.sting('goal', { at: 'bar' })` | a 2-bar fanfare |\n1016:| `tension` | shootouts, the Save Duel | a held chord and a heartbeat (the kick drum at 60 bpm) |\n1018:| `villain` | Baron von Bullion's scenes | a minor, oily waltz |\n1019:| `ceremony` | the trophy lift | the anthem, full and fast |\n1020:| `credits` | credits, the album | the anthem as a music box (triangle and sine) |\n1021:| `training` | training | a laid-back loop |\n1022:| `attract` | attract mode | the anthem's high-energy remix |\n1337:|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1338:| 1 | WALLY CRABB | GK | bulky 1.2, bald | keep 76, weight 80 | 41, a part-time lighthouse keeper; huge gloves |\n1339:| 4 | SANDRA \"THE HARBOUR WALL\" OKAFOR | DEF | bulky 1.2, short | tackle 88, weight 95, temper 40 | barges like a trawler |\n1340:| 6 | AGGIE NOWAK | MID | heroic 1.12, ponytail | pass 90, skill 70 | the brains; Polish grandmother in the stands |\n1341:| 7 | TOMMY \"TWINKLETOES\" TRAN | FWD | heroic 1.08, spiky | pace 95, skill 92 | step-overs for breakfast |\n1342:| 9 | DAZ PILCHARD (captain) | FWD | heroic 1.15, short | shoot 90, pace 80 | super **THE SMOKED KIPPER** (path `wobble`, smoke trail, the ball briefly shaped like a fish) |\n1349:|---|---|---|---|\n1350:| 1 | ALF STOPPARD | GK | long kicks only |\n1351:| 3 | GAZ HOOPER | DEF | heads everything |\n1352:| 5 | DUNCAN DUNSTABLE | DEF | bulky; weight 92 |\n1353:| 8 | KEV LUMP | MID | \"Lump it!\" |\n1354:| 9 | NORMAN \"THE NODDER\" NEEDHAM (captain) | FWD | headers 95; super **ROW Z RETURN** (`meteor`: a hoof into the sky that comes down onto the goal) |\n1361:|---|---|---|---|\n1362:| 1 | PACO PORTERO | GK | |\n1363:| 4 | RAFA RONDO | DEF | |\n1364:| 6 | TITO TOQUE | MID | one touch, always |\n1365:| 8 | IKER INTERIOR | MID | |\n1366:| 10 | PEPITO PASARELA (captain) | MID | chibi build 1.0 (tiny); super **EL PASODOBLE** (`zigzag`: the ball dances 3 steps in rhythm) |\n1373:|---|---|---|---|\n1374:| 1 | MANNI MAUER | GK | |\n1375:| 2 | FRANZI FLEISS | DEF | never stops running |\n1376:| 5 | UWE UMSCHALT | MID | transitions |\n1377:| 7 | JURGEN JAGD (JÜRGEN once §5.5 lands) | FWD | the hunter |\n1378:| 9 | KLAUS HAMMERSCHMIDT (captain) | FWD | bulky 1.25; super **DER HAMMERSCHLAG** (`hammer`: 3 forge-hammer bounces, each shaking the screen) |\n....\n### 7.3 The story (Cup Run beats)\n\nThe premise: the Continental Federation meant to invite KINGSBRIDGE ALBION to the EUROPHORIA CUP, Europe's grandest\nknockout competition. A clerk typed KIPPERTON instead, and the rules say an invitation is an invitation. Kipperton\nAthletic (population 3,112; floodlights powered by fish oil; fourteen pounds in the kitty) are going to Europe in a\nminibus with three good tyres.\n\n**Prologue** (`prologue`)\n- Tabloid, THE DAILY ROAR: **\"FISH OUT OF WATER!\"** — \"Typo sends tiny Kipperton into the Europhoria Cup. 'Rules are\n  rules,' shrugs the Federation.\"\n- Talk at the Smokehouse:\n  - MAGS: \"Right, you lot. Fourteen quid in the kitty, a minibus with three good tyres, and a letter that says EUROPE.\"\n  - DAZ: \"Gaffer, do they have chips in Europe?\"\n  - MAGS: \"They have EVERYTHING in Europe, Darren. Including teams that'll eat us for breakfast.\"\n  - SANDRA: \"Let 'em try. I've got an appetite and all.\"\n  - MAGS: \"That's the spirit. First up, at home: AFC Hoofington. Route-one merchants. Keep your heads up. Literally.\"\n  - Choice: [ \"LET'S PLAY\" ] / [ \"TRAINING FIRST\" ] (the second goes to Training, then back to the cup).\n\n**Qualifying Round** — vs AFC Hoofington at the Smokehouse (rain, dusk). Referee Haltwhistle.\n- Pre: **\"THE LONG AND THE SHORT OF IT\"** — \"Hoofington's aerial bombardment heads for Kipperton's puddles.\"\n- NEEDHAM (on a portrait card): \"We don't pass, love. We 'oof.\"\n- Challenge: **Score a header.**\n- Win: **\"KIP KIP HOORAY!\"**; loss: **\"BATTERED!\"**\n- After: MAGS: \"Not bad. Not good. But not bad.\" TREV (a commentary card): \"A proper cold night, and they've warmed it up.\"\n\n**Round of 16** — vs Real Pasapasa at Estadio Pasapasa (sun). Referee Patience.\n- Travel: the minibus heads south, with a postcard: \"WISH YOU WERE HERE (IT'S HOT)\".\n- Pre: **\"PASS THE PARCEL\"** — \"Kippers must stop the passing masters... if they can find the ball.\"\n- PEPITO: \"You will chase the ball until you are dizzy, little fishes.\"\n- Challenge: **Win the ball back 5 times.**\n- Win: **\"SOLE-DESTROYING FOR SOLERA!\"**; loss: **\"PASSED OUT\"**\n- After: AGGIE: \"I counted. They made 412 passes.\" MAGS: \"And we made two goals. Football's a funny old game.\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4140afa2-f753-4694-9098-5b15dffc61f3","uuid":"d49b87fb-8452-4c17-925c-c9b5467dda54","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:36:55.745Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 7.1 Teams\n\nEach team: name, short code, nickname, city, stadium, kits (home, away, keeper), crest, formation, tactic, chant,\nsignature celebration, 5 players (number, name, position, build, size, hair, skin, hair colour, stats, captain's super).\nKit colours give rig colours: `cloth` (shirt), `pants` (shorts), `boot`, `belt` (= shorts), `trim` (socks and collar),\n`glove` (keepers), plus `kit: { pattern, color2, number, numberColor }` (§5.2).\n\n**KIPPERTON ATHLETIC** — \"The Kippers\", KIP. A fishing town on the cold north coast. Home: the Smokehouse. Kit: tangerine\n`#f08a24` and navy `#1c2a5a` hoops, navy shorts, tangerine socks; away: white with a tangerine sash. Crest: a navy shield\nwith a smoked kipper crossed over an anchor. Formation 2-1-1 (the team talk can change it). Tactic `plucky` (balanced:\npress .55, line .45, tempo .7, passRisk .5). Chant \"KIP-PER-TON!\". Celebration: the fish slap. Manager: MAGS MULLIGAN\n(a fishmonger turned manager: flat cap, scarf, a voice like a foghorn).\n\n| # | Name | Pos | Build / size / hair | Key stats | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | WALLY CRABB | GK | bulky 1.2, bald | keep 76, weight 80 | 41, a part-time lighthouse keeper; huge gloves |\n| 4 | SANDRA \"THE HARBOUR WALL\" OKAFOR | DEF | bulky 1.2, short | tackle 88, weight 95, temper 40 | barges like a trawler |\n| 6 | AGGIE NOWAK | MID | heroic 1.12, ponytail | pass 90, skill 70 | the brains; Polish grandmother in the stands |\n| 7 | TOMMY \"TWINKLETOES\" TRAN | FWD | heroic 1.08, spiky | pace 95, skill 92 | step-overs for breakfast |\n| 9 | DAZ PILCHARD (captain) | FWD | heroic 1.15, short | shoot 90, pace 80 | super **THE SMOKED KIPPER** (path `wobble`, smoke trail, the ball briefly shaped like a fish) |\n\n**AFC HOOFINGTON** — \"The Hoofers\", HOO (Qualifying Round). Brown `#6a4a2a` and amber `#e8a830` stripes. Crest: a\nmuddy boot. Formation 2-2. Tactic `routeone` (longBall .6, press .4, line .4, tempo .5, foul .25). Chant: a\n....\n11:|---|---|\n77:|---|---|\n98:|---|---|---|\n119:|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n120:| move | run / dribble | run | L-stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n121:| `sprint` | sprint (stamina) | sprint | R2 / RT (`Pad7`) | Left Shift | — |\n122:| `pass` | ground pass to the teammate the stick points at | standing tackle (poke) | ✕ / A (`Pad0`) | J | Left click: pass toward the cursor (click a teammate to pass to them) |\n123:| `shoot` | hold to charge, release to shoot; stick aims | slide tackle | □ / X (`Pad2`) | K | Right button held: charge, release to shoot at the cursor |\n124:| `lob` | lob, cross from wide, chip near the keeper | shoulder barge | ○ / B (`Pad1`) | L | Middle click: lob toward the cursor |\n125:| `through` | through ball into space | switch player | △ / Y (`Pad3`) | I | —