{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BrdD9QDmvop7tf2C1ERUn","type":"tool_result","content":"139:- `down(a)`, `pressed(a)`, `released(a)`, `repeat(a, delay, rate)` (menus), `buffered(a, win)` + `consume(a)`, `consumeAll()`, `anyPressed()`, `move()` (screen direction `[x, y]`, length up to 1), `use(preset)`, `touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'])`, `touchSet('confirm', 'TALK', near)` (a context button: relabel it, or hide it while it has nothing to do).\n143:- Controller settings: `deadzone` (default `.18`, radial and rescaled), `invertAimY`, `lastDevice` (the index has the rest). The left stick and the touch stick, pushed past halfway, press `up` / `down` / `left` / `right` as the d-pad does (menus, dialog choices, ladders); bind `PadAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` to your own menu actions for the same.\n....\n131:- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`. `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the screen (or null): keep a HUD clear of it.\n132:- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)` (0, 1, 2 or `'auto'`), `load(slot)`, `copy(a, b)`, `erase(slot)`, `autosave()`, `list()`, `latest()` (a title's Continue). `menu: { saves: true }` (or `{ slots, version, migrate(data, from) }`) puts Save (while `saves.canSave`: a save point) and Load in the pause menu, and `saves.show('save' | 'load')` opens the screen from your own menu. Blocked storage keeps them for the visit.\n....\n849:   *  (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER,\n853:    if (typeof map === 'string') map = Input[map.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT;\n866:    /** preset: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own) */\n1014:  _check(a) { if (!this.map[a]) warn('action:' + a, 'unknown input action \"' + a + '\". Known actions: ' + Object.keys(this.map).join(', ') + '. Add your own with new E.Game({ input: { ...E.Input.DEFAULT, ' + a + \": ['KeyQ'] } })\"); }\n1275:Input.DEFAULT = {\n....\n912:  label(a, device = this.lastDevice) {\n1010:  tap(a) { if (!this.map[a]) { this._check(a); return; } this._tapCode('Act:' + a); }\n1013:  hold(a, on = true) { if (!this.map[a]) { this._check(a); return; } if (on) this.press('Act:' + a); else this.release('Act:' + a); }\n1016:  down(a) { const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return false; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return false; for (const c of m) if (this.held.has(c)) return true; return false; }\n1018:  pressed(a) { if (!this.map[a]) this._check(a); return !this._suppressed.has(a) && this._now.has(a); }\n1020:  released(a) { return this._nowUp.has(a); }\n1032:  consume(a) { this._used[a] = true; }\n1040:  consumeAll() { for (const a in this.map) this._used[a] = true; this._now.clear(); this._fresh.clear(); this._clickAt = this._click = null; }\n1055:  move() {\n6197:  move(b, dt, solids) {\n7715:      tap(perf) {\n11219:  move(b, dt) {\n14502:  label() { return 'DAY ' + this.day + '  ' + String(this.hour).padStart(2, '0') + ':' + String(Math.floor(this.minute / 10) * 10).padStart(2, '0'); }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4140afa2-f753-4694-9098-5b15dffc61f3","uuid":"b5e3656b-aada-455b-8ea0-918d9a0607fa","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:37:07.877Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"139:- `down(a)`, `pressed(a)`, `released(a)`, `repeat(a, delay, rate)` (menus), `buffered(a, win)` + `consume(a)`, `consumeAll()`, `anyPresse